# Git: fetch before any activity

Cloud Agents / iPhone merges update **GitHub only**. Local and agent checkouts can be behind `origin`. Never start git work on a stale view of the repo.

## Mandatory before git activity

Before **any** of the following, run `git fetch --all --prune` first (or `git fetch origin` if that is the only remote):

- Inspecting branch state for a decision (`status`, `log`, `diff` vs remote)
- Committing
- Merging / rebasing
- Pushing
- Creating or syncing `develop` ↔ `main`
- “Checkin / merge / sync” style user requests
- Any command that could move branch tips or overwrite remote history

After fetch, sync the branch you will change:

```bash
git fetch --all --prune
git status -sb
# If behind origin on the working branch:
git pull --ff-only
# or: git merge --ff-only @{u}
```

Prefer **fast-forward only** pulls/merges unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.

## Do not

- Commit or push based on a pre-fetch assumption that local `develop`/`main` match GitHub
- Force-push or reset in ways that discard remote commits
- Merge `develop` → `main` (or the reverse) without fetching both tips first
- Assume an iPhone / Cloud Agent merge is already on the local machine

## After remote merges (phone / cloud)

Remind or run fetch/pull on the local workspace so the Mac checkout matches `origin` before further local edits.
